# Single source of truth for the vendored `helm` pin. TWO independent consumers, one pin (the
# cosign/skopeo pin discipline):
#   - apps/stackd (M29.4, ADR-0058) — the stack controller renders `deploy/helm-bundled` with THIS
#     binary, in-process, and never downloads one at runtime.
#   - apps/runner-dep-vendor (M29.8a, ADR-0059) — the credential-free re-vendor sandbox's `helm
#     template` step for Gitea's chart (network-none once built; this stage is the one place in
#     that image's build that reaches the network at all).
#
# Shell-sourceable (`. tools/helm/pin.env`) AND parsed verbatim by:
#   - apps/stackd/Dockerfile               (ARG defaults — must match the three values below)
#   - apps/stackd/src/helm.ts              (fail-closed version assertion at startup; the image
#                                           copies this file next to the binary)
#   - apps/runner-dep-vendor/Dockerfile    (ARG HELM_PINNED_VERSION / HELM_TARBALL_SHA256 defaults)
#   - scripts/install-pinned-helm.sh       (CI installs THIS binary, verified by sha256)
# `apps/stackd/src/helm-pin.test.ts` asserts the stackd Dockerfile agrees with this file.
#
# Why a release tarball and not an image (the cosign/skopeo pins take the binary from the upstream
# project's own image): the Helm project publishes no official container image. The official
# distribution is the get.helm.sh tarball plus its published sha256, so that is what is pinned.
#
# HELM 3, NOT HELM 4 (recorded, not an oversight — re-check before bumping past 3.x).
# `tools/vendor-refresh/src/gitea-plan.ts` was built and tested entirely against Helm 3's `helm
# template` output shape (its Secret/hook-annotation parsing, `# Source:` comment stripping).
# Moving to Helm 4 needs that compatibility re-verified against a real Helm 4 render before the pin
# follows — a separate, deliberate piece of work, not a version bump.

# The version `helm version --template '{{.Version}}'` reports.
HELM_PINNED_VERSION=v3.20.2

# sha256 of helm-${HELM_PINNED_VERSION}-linux-amd64.tar.gz, from get.helm.sh's own .sha256sum file
# (fetched 2026-09-24). linux/amd64 only, like every other pin here.
HELM_TARBALL_SHA256=258e830a9e613c8a7a302d6059b4bb3b9758f2f3e1bb8ea0d707ce10a9a72fea

# Where the binary lives inside the scp-stackd image — deliberately not /usr/local/bin, so an
# operator-installed helm is never mistaken for the vetted pin. Not used by runner-dep-vendor,
# which installs it at /helm-bin/helm inside its own build stage.
HELM_VENDORED_PATH=/opt/scp/bin/helm
